    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/EmailReadingPaneShell/__tests__/EmailReadingPaneShell.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the shell mounts with Email items, when it renders, then the reused `PanelSplitter` shows the `EmailCardList` on the left and the reading pane on the right (resizable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a card is clicked, when `onSelect(id)` fires, then the shell's `selectedId` updates and the right-pane body/header slots are invoked with that id (selection drives the right pane).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given nothing is selected, when the shell renders, then the right pane shows the "Select an email" placeholder (FR-19).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the splitter is resized, when the shell is re-mounted, then the previously set width is restored from the persisted key.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a selected email, when the reading pane renders, then a single full-width toolbar spans the reading-pane width with Reply / Reply All / Forward / New / Archive / Create, each wired to dispatch through the extracted `CommunicationActions` (022) core (compose behavior itself lands in 036).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the downstream sub-views (033/034/035/036), when they compose in, then they fill the shell's named slots without editing the shell (slot contract holds).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a host `FluentProvider` in dark theme, when the shell renders, then all chrome uses tokens (ADR-021 dark mode) and no `as React.ComponentType` cast is introduced (NFR-05).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build` for `@spaarke/communication-components` is green and all new tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference spec FR-05 + FR-08 + FR-19 and design Lens 2 (two-pane, selection→right pane, full-width toolbar) + Lens 4 (BUILD verdict). This shell is the composition root for the P3b wave (033 body / 034 header+attachments / 035 connections+tracking / 036 compose+Open-full-form) — hence `parallel-safe:false`: it must land before P3b so those tasks fill its slots. Toolbar dispatch reuses task 022's extracted `CommunicationActions` logic (FR-08), NOT a forked action bar. "Open full form" (85% `navigateTo` modal) is task 036. Completion summary appended here when done.</notes>

